Lane R (PASS 87, HF-423) — publish-guard patch, REPORTED, NOT APPLIED.

scripts/orchestration/publish_pass*.py is owned by the integration lane, so this
lane does not edit it. This is the exact change to make in publish_pass87.py
(which will be derived from publish_pass85.py — the guard, its red test and both
call sites are unchanged there since PASS 84).

WHY IT HAS TO CHANGE
--------------------
`assert_farcrysis_not_selectable` refuses to publish any tree whose farcrysis
registry entry is missing `selectable:!1`. HF-423 makes farcrysis selectable as a
PREVIEW card, so that guard will REFUSE the PASS 87 tree by design. It must not
simply be deleted: it is the only thing standing between the menu and an arena
that once cold-loaded in 279 s and killed the tab. Replace it with a guard that
is strictly harder to satisfy — a flag can be flipped in one line, a receipt has
to be earned by running the arena.

The replacement reads the receipt this lane's collector writes:
  node scripts/qa/collect-farcrysis-admission-evidence.mjs --runs 3
  -> docs/evidence/pass87/lane-r/farcrysis-admission.json
    (contract farcrysis-admission-evidence-v1)

The ceiling is a RATIO against an atomic-acres control measured in the SAME
machine window, never an absolute millisecond budget. That is deliberate: an
absolute budget is a fence, and a fence that has to be widened whenever the
owner's ComfyUI is busy is a fence that has been widened. The pair ratio is
immune to that, because a busy machine slows the control too.

